# E85: a variable ethanol blend

@left

![Flex-fuel vehicle badge](assets/lect06c-set_4_tp_chapter_12_16_material/image_016.png)

@right

- U.S. E85 contains 51-83% ethanol, depending on season and location.
- Ethanol can be produced by fermenting sugars from corn starch.
- It contains less energy per gallon than gasoline.

[DOE: ethanol blends](https://afdc.energy.gov/fuels/ethanol-e85)

@notes

Source: lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 18.
