# Switchgrass

@left

![Slide image 26](assets/lect06c-set_4_tp_chapter_12_16_material/image_026.png)

@right

- dominant species of the central N.A. tallgrass prairie
- versatile and adaptable plant – thrives in many weather conditions, seasons lengths, soil types, and land conditions
- used primarily for soil conservation – deep root system leave a rich layer of organic matter in the Midwest U.S. soil
- ability to produce moderate to high yields on marginal farmlands

