=== layout: two-panels

# Introducing genes into plants

@left

## Agrobacterium

- Transfer engineered T-DNA into plant cells.
- Ti-plasmid-based systems in culture
- Floral dip in suitable species

@right

## Particle bombardment

- Deliver DNA on small particles.
- Often uses gold particles
- Accelerated into plant tissue

@notes

Source: lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 66.
Converted layout or wording reviewed against the original slide. Original text and import diagnostics are retained in the review evidence.

=== layout: one-panel

# Methods for introducing genes into plant cells

@body

- Two lesser known methods\:
  - #3 Protoplast system – remove the cell wall, add DNA, regenerate plant cells
  - #4 Electroporation – an electrical field is applied to increase membrane permeability and allow DNA to be introduced into the cell.

@notes

Source: lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 67.
